 "issue": 223,
 "issue_title": "Optimizer checks rim, ignores vertex collapse \u2014 designs inside-out lenses",
 "issue_body": "**Files:** `src/optimizer.py:254-260`, `src/analysis/plots.py:64-71`\n\n```python\nedge_thickness = lens.thickness - s1 + s2\nif edge_thickness < min_et: merit += 1e4*(min_et-edge_thickness)**2\n```\n\nThis is only rim thickness (under the `plots.py` rim-convention: `x2_edge=x1_edge+thickness`). Vertex separation `thickness + s1 - s2` is never checked.\n\nKill shot: `s1=-20, s2=+20, thickness=5` \u2192 `edge=45mm` passes, but `vertex=-35mm` \u2014 front vertex 35mm behind back vertex, lens inside-out. Optimizer rewards it.\n\n**Fix:**\n```python\ncenter = lens.thickness + s1 - s2\nif center < min_ct: merit += 1e5*(min_ct-center)**2\nif center <= 0: merit += 1e8  # hard infeasible\n```\nDecide once whether `Lens.thickness` is rim or vertex distance \u2014 currently docstring says rim, every optics textbook says vertex.\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/pmaasz/openLens/issues/223",
 "pr": 235,
 "pr_title": "fix(optimizer): reject vertex collapse and align viz to center-thickn\u2026",
 "pr_body": "\u2026ess convention\r\n\r\nHarden MeritFunction._penalty_physical with hard 1e8 penalties for center<=0, edge<=0, invalid sag |R|<h, interior meniscus self-intersection, and edge-clearance violations.\r\n\r\n- Define Lens.thickness as CENTER (vertex-to-vertex) thickness; derive rim thickness as thickness - sag1 + sag2\r\n- Align outlines in plots, lens_viz_2d/3d, simulation_viz, assembly_viz to vertex convention\r\n- Apply black formatting to touched files",
 "fix_commit": "f0956e64c2a86a28dbc9b1b31b33d992a94c7956",
